      "prompt": "Add optional aliases to click.Choice through a new aliases=None constructor parameter. aliases is a mapping from string alias names to exact string members of the original choices; copy the mapping so caller mutation cannot change the type. Reject non-mappings, non-string keys or values, and targets outside the original choices with ValueError at construction. Accept aliases during conversion and return the original canonical choice object. Apply Context.token_normalize_func followed by case folding when case_sensitive=False to both user input and aliases, just as for canonical choices. If normalized aliases collide with another alias or canonical name mapping to a different canonical choice, raise BadParameter during conversion rather than silently choosing one; collisions mapping to the same target are allowed. Preserve behavior without aliases. Help, invalid-input choice lists, and shell completion must continue to show canonical choices only. Add regression tests.",
